# Constant adaptation for tests/contract/mathck_mixed_width.sh (G3):
# dialect|setting|statement|expected stdout, or "reject <op>" for a G24
# rejection (exact mixed_admission.err with that operator, no executable)
# |derivation. The suite fills mixed_constants.pas; the extended dialect
# adds a: INTEGER32; d: WORD32 (both 5). An INTEGER constant adapts to a
# WORD operand by its bit pattern, so the adapted unsigned arithmetic wraps
# under MATHCK- (IBM 8-4: WRD(C) + -1 overflows). A WORD constant adapts
# to a signed operand only if it fits.
vintage|-|WRITELN(w + (-1), w - NEG, NEG + w)|464|WRD(-1) = 65535: 5 + 65535 wraps to 4; 5 - 65535 wraps to 6; 65535 + 5 wraps to 4
vintage|-|WRITELN(w + WRD(i), WRD(i) - w)|365529|WRD(-2) = 65534: 5 + 65534 = 65539 wraps to 3; 65534 - 5 = 65529
vintage|+|WRITELN(i + 30000, w + 30000)|2999830005|-2 + 30000 = 29998; 5 + 30000 = 30005
extended|+|WRITELN(a + 40000, 40000 * a, a - BIG)|40005200000-39995|5 + 40000 = 40005; 40000 * 5 = 200000; 5 - 40000 = -39995
extended|-|WRITELN(d - NEG, d + (-1))|64|WRD32(-1) adapts by bit pattern: 5 - (2^32 - 1) and 5 + (2^32 - 1) wrap to 6 and 4
vintage|+|WRITELN(i + BIG)|reject +|BIG = 40000 does not fit INTEGER, so it stays WORD: G24
vintage|+|WRITELN(40000 - i)|reject -|40000 does not fit INTEGER: G24
